## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an edge-friendly, few-shot adaptable vision system with robust localization under real-time constraints and production-domain data shifts.

## Key Concepts

- Edge-efficient architectures, few-shot adapters
- Synthetic+real data for defect distribution
- Temporal consistency and localization losses

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass outline
function forward(frame, adapter) {
  const feat = backbone(frame);
  const heatmap = detectorHead(feat);
  const adapted = adapter(feat);
  const localized = fuse(heatmap, adapted);
  return localized;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate real-time performance on hardware with varying thermal conditions?
- What failure modes require monitoring in production and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical monocular depth reasoning and tracking in a simple inspection setting.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth proxy with known geometry
- Lightweight detectors, on-device adaptation
- Temporal tracking and data efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
function projectTo3D(bbox, sheetDims, intrinsics) {
  // heuristic: depth proxy from vertical size and known sheet height
  const heightPx = bbox.height;
  const Z = (sheetDims.height * intrinsics.fy) / heightPx;
  return {X: 0, Y: 0, Z};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would occlusion or specular glare affect depth proxy? how to mitigate?
- How would you measure success and compare to a stereo baseline?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests real-time monocular depth, multi-task learning, and pose estimation in a challenging forest domain, plus on-device few-shot adaptation and map fusion.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth and semantic/instance segmentation
- 6-DoF pose estimation for markers
- TSDF fusion for map building on edge hardware
- Differentiable rendering for domain adaptation
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
class MonocularDroneNet {
  constructor(){ /* backbone */ }
  forward(frame){
    const depth = this.depthHead(frameFeatures)
    const segPose = this.segPoseHead(frameFeatures)
    const pose = this.markerPoseHead(segPose)
    const map = this.tsdfFuse(depth, pose)
    return {depth, segPose, pose, map}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ablate temporal consistency vs per-frame independence?
- What data policies ensure robust marker generalization across weekly styles?
- How would you monitor edge latency under CPU/GPU contention?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to architect privacy-aware computer vision systems under strict edge constraints while balancing accuracy and privacy guarantees. Requires concrete architecture, differentiable privacy terms, and rigorous evaluation plans.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving CV and de-identification modules
- Differentiable privacy loss and threat-model-aware evaluation
- Edge/on-device inference and latency budgeting
- Trade-offs between detection accuracy and privacy guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight total loss combining detection accuracy and privacy
function computeTotalLoss(detectionPred, privacyPred, targets) {
    const detectionLoss = computeDetectionLoss(detectionPred, targets);
    const privacyLoss = computePrivacyLoss(privacyPred, targets.sensitiveRegions);

    // Weighted combination with privacy budget constraint
    return detectionLoss + lambdaPrivacy * privacyLoss;
}

// Differentiable de-identification module
class PrivacyModule {
    obfuscate(features, sensitiveRegions) {
        // Apply learnable obfuscation to sensitive regions
        return features.map((feat, i) => 
            sensitiveRegions[i] ? this.anonymize(feat) : feat
        );
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a practical, low-latency perception and manipulation system that must rapidly adapt to new furniture models while maintaining consistent performance across different camera configurations—a critical constraint in consumer robotics applications.

## Key Concepts
- 6-DoF pose estimation from monocular RGB
- 5-shot on-device adaptation strategies
- Cross-camera intrinsics handling techniques
- Synthetic-to-real data augmentation approaches
- Embedded GPU latency optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: estimate pose with adaptation
function estimatePoseWithAdaptation(rgbFrame, newFurnitureSamples) {
  // Detect furniture in RGB frame
  const detections = furnitureDetector.predict(rgbFrame);

  // Adapt to new furniture with 5-shot learning
  if (newFurnitureSamples.length >= 5) {
    metaLearner.adapt(newFurnitureSamples);
  }

  // Estimate 6-DoF pose using PnP
  const poses = detections.map(detection => 
    solvePnP(detection.keypoints, detection.3dModel, normalizedIntrinsics)
  );

  return { poses, detections };
}
```
